Z||000000||yo_sweet||10-29-2001||01:28 PM||||i was at a local yard today and i found a third gen trans am with side scoops so i popped them off and asked the the guy how much he said $40 cnd!!!!!,then he has the nerve to tell me it was cheap and i was getting a deal, what an a$$hole and he woulden't budge down so im like f*ck this ****  , its crazy not to mention this guy is not lisenced to sell parts and he gets the cars for free , btw in the summer i went there to buy a winshelid i was cutting it out and the blade slipped and it shattered he charged me $70 <P>------------------<BR>1986 Fiero SE<BR>customized tail light's,american raceing rim's,k&n air filter,pioneer cd player.. more to come<P>kill's: 1990 Honda CRX,93 ACURA integra, 85 mr2,94 pontiac grand am,94 mustang, suzuki swift 5 car lengths!,86 laser 4cyl.<P>loses: 1996 camero Z28,2000 grand prix 3.8L, 1986 monty carlo SS||||reg||8
Z||000001||FieroJoe||10-29-2001||01:31 PM||||Well, it <B>is</B> a business, and his price dosent sound too un reasonable.<P>If you didnt like him in the first place why did you go back?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula88||10-29-2001||02:32 PM||||Yeah - those cars in the yard are his inventory.  Doesn't matter if he paid for them or not.  He's trying to run a business and make a living.  If his prices are too high, get your parts somewhere else.  If you can't find them somewhere else or cheaper, his prices must be about right then, huh?<P>We all like to find bargains, but what were you expecting?  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||10-29-2001||03:00 PM||||Most yards I deal with wont sell front or rear window glass period. If you broke it I can understand him charging you. I go for new. I pay $115 for Fiero windshields brand new and installed. You spent $70 and even if you got it out would it have been worth $45 more to not have to bother with it? I deal with yards almost everyday with my shop. I found that a lot of time, you can get a brand new item for less than yard asks. I pulled a Fiero speedometer just to get the needle, and they wanted $50....no tks. Another ex, I needed a newer caddy rear bumper, yard wanted $750 complete (3 pcs) but buying the 3 parts separate from caddy dealer cost me $515 new. So dont think that just because its junkyard stuff your getting a bargain. check around first.||||reg||1
Z||000004||ChopTop||10-29-2001||03:58 PM||||Yep, we have a salvage yard like that here too.  I learned real quick to ask the price BEFORE I attempted to pulled it.  I also learned forum members prices are generally a heck of a lot lower.  For some it's a business for others a hobby.||||reg||1
